(EventNote ev-ep-note-20260903T163039Z "PERF-PATCH 09-03 09:29 (_petta_journal.resolve_supersedes): hoisted 2 regexes to module-level compiled patterns (_RE_SUPERSEDES, _RE_MEMORY_CLUSTER) + substring prefilter ((Supersedes/(MemoryCluster not in line -> skip), so regexes only run on candidate lines. Motivation: resolve slowed 0.32ms (1099 lines, ep-tail-16) -> 3.95ms (1486 lines) as the append-only journal grows; profile showed cost was regex re-dispatch (30k re._compile cache hits/20 runs) + per-line re.match/finditer, NOT compile — cache was being hit but lookup overhead dominated. Equivalence-verified: patched output byte-identical to pre-patch backup (/tmp/_petta_journal_backup_0903_0929.py) on the real journal AND 5 synthetic edge cases (placeholder Supersedes new-id/old-id, real cluster-drop, Supersedes-inside-quoted-string text-level behavior, empty, self-supersede). Result: 3.95 -> 0.62 ms/resolve (6.4x), 50-run avg. recall() path (read+resolve) now cheap enough for per-wakeup context injection at journal sizes well beyond current.")
;;; END MemoryCluster ep-note-20260903T163039Z
